# SEBI Regulatory Unit

Single rule for **SEBI Investment Adviser** work. Three modes — use the section that matches the task.

**Sources:** `docs/SEBI_COMPLIANCE_CHECKLIST.md` · `docs/SEBI_PROCESS_INSTRUCTIONS.md` · `docs/regulatory/INDEX.md` · `docs/ACCESSIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md`

---

## 1. Feature compliance (when building)

Applies when code touches **clients, advice, agreements, disclosures, risk profiling, or reporting**.

### Record-keeping & suitability
- No silent overwrites — append, version, or log changes (who/when).
- Store agreements, risk profile + date, suitability, recommendations (generated/sent/executed), key communications.
- Link recommendations to risk profile; if override allowed, store **override reason** and **approver**.

### Disclosures & conduct
- Capture what was disclosed, to whom, when. Agreements: signed copy, version, client_id, date, audit link.
- Advisor actions traceable to user + timestamp.

### Audit trail
- Log login/logout, password change, client/portfolio access, downloads, recommendation send/execute, client/advice CRUD.
- Use `services/audit_service.log_audit_event(...)` and `AuditLog` model.

### Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- Semantic HTML, keyboard nav, form labels, errors with `role="alert"`, no color-only meaning, accessible PDFs.

### Per-feature checklist
- [ ] Records auditable (no silent overwrites)?
- [ ] Suitability / risk profile considered for advice?
- [ ] Disclosures captured?
- [ ] Critical actions audit-logged?
- [ ] Regulator can export evidence from stored data?
- [ ] Relevant circulars checked in `docs/regulatory/INDEX.md`?

